  "text": "Thank you all for raising these concerns — they're all significant and need to be addressed before we publish. Let me summarize what I'm hearing: Owen, we need to account for the privileged Docker-in-Docker requirement in the release pipeline by adding two isolated persistent runners alongside the ephemeral runners. Lena, our observed burst of 28 concurrent jobs exceeds the draft's 20-job limit, and we need to raise the cap and set up alerting at the 24-job threshold, staying within the 32-job safe ceiling. Ravi, the compliance requirements for regulated repositories demand 180-day immutable log retention and signed provenance attestations, which the current draft doesn't cover. All three of these are blocking issues for me. Before I settle on a final policy, I want to confirm a couple of things: Owen, can you update the platform proposal with the two-persistent-runner design so we can review it? Lena, can you get those measurements onto the capacity dashboard and confirm the alerting can be configured at the 24-job threshold? Ravi, can you open the compliance ticket so we have a formal record? Once those are in motion, I'll draft a revised policy incorporating all three concerns and circulate it for a final review before publishing."
}
